@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: CSE Routing
	Testing the routing of specific tickets to CSE user groups

Teardown:
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| User1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Organization1 |

Scenario: CSE BR PT Routing
	End users who create requests for a Brazil support organization with Portuguese as the support language for specific products and components should have their requests routed to the CSE - BR - PT group.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | Regular             |
	| Support Region   | Brazil              |
	| Support Language | Portuguese          | 
	| External ID      | Organization1       |
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "Organization1" with the following tags
	| developer_tools         |
	| enterprise_search       |
	| liferay_commerce        |
	| liferay_dxp             |
	| liferay_portal          |
	| management_tools_lcs    |
	| mobile_device_detection |
	| mobile_experience       |
	| productivity_tools_sync |
	| social_office           |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Portuguese                       |
	| Time Zone        | Brasilia                         | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_developer_tools         |                                        |
	| prd_enterprise_search       |                                        |
	| prd_liferay_commerce        | apis_integrations_and_extension_points |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_1         | apio_architect                         |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_0         | application_display_templates          |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2      | authentication                         |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_1      | caching_clustering                     |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_0      | calendar                               |
	| prd_liferay_portal_5_2      | collaboration_suite                    |
	| prd_management_tools_lcs    |                                        |
	| prd_mobile_device_detection |                                        |
	| prd_mobile_experience       |                                        |
	| prd_productivity_tools_sync |                                        |
	| prd_social_office           |                                        |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be assigned to the group "CSE - BR - PT - General"

